  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening NGOs&apos; as well as Local and Diaspora-led CSOs&#x2019; Capacities on Preparedness and Emergency Response in the Context of Mixed Migration Flows in LAC and Shelter Support for Migrants and Host Communities in Ecuador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed intervention aims to strengthen Non-Governmental Organizations&#x2019; (NGOs), local and diaspora-led Civil Society Organizations&#x2019; (CSOs) preparedness capacities and ability to meet critical humanitarian and protection needs of the most vulnerable migrant and refugee populations in Latin America and the Caribbean (LAC). The project focuses on four results: 1) institutional strengthening and development of NGOs, local and diaspora-led CSOs&#x2019; capacities to provide emergency assistance and protection across the LAC region, particularly in Chile, Peru, Ecuador Dominican Republic, and Panama; 2) in kind support to strengthen 10 selected NGOs, local and diaspora-led CSOs&#x2019; humanitarian assistance service provision in the five abovementioned countries; 3) direct life-saving assistance to migrants and refugees affected by an unforeseen crisis; and 4) improvement and/or adaptation of infrastructure for collective shelters that meet the standards required to provide shelter and protection services in addition to being environmentally sustainable. IOM and the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights (OHCHR) are collaborating with NGOs and CSOs operating in the region to provide capacity building on humanitarian and protection issues and direct material assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
